{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1161970-expanding-on-twilight","id":1161970,"title":"Expanding on Twilight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-23T14:35:13-08:00","id":1161970,"title":"Expanding on Twilight","content":"I have a slight issue in my current game. The players have taken to using Twilight (the Death phase, specifically) as, essentially, &quot;stealth mode&quot;, turning them invisible and intangible to everyone in the physical realm.<br /> <br /> Now, this is largely supported by the book, which states entities in Twilight are invisible and intangible, but can see and hear the physical realm (though it would be distorted enough to not work as a way to spy on people)<br /> <br /> This largely eliminates any threat in the physical realm, which is fine. However, there is no &quot;cost&quot;, aside from 3 seconds of casting and a chance die of paradox.<br /> <br /> The question, then, is how do I expand on the concept of Twilight as described in the books to be interesting?<br /> <br /> Ghosts could be more numerous, but if there is several ghosts within eyeshot always in Twilight, they become bland scenery. I favor the idea that ghosts are rarer and more &quot;colourful&quot;, having a personality, reliving their death in some detail, but I suppose that could be combined with the faceless drifting spectres drifting through Twilight, to still give some &quot;movement&quot; to Twilight.<br /> <br /> The intangibility is in part solved by Ephemeral Enchantment, perhaps a Death 2 shielding spell to make a wall in the physical realm tangible in Twilight (A Ban would work with Death 2 if you want to create a barrier not tied to a physical object), but I remember, perhaps from 1e, locations tied to the corresponding Arcanum, e.g. a house where someone was murdered, would be tangible in Twilight. This ties nicely together with the more powerful ghosts, where the lair of a powerful ghost will be tangible in Twilight (though it may no longer exist in the real world)<br /> <br /> There's also the question of just how invisible they are. Death 1 would be able to see into Death Twilight, but is that the only way? I spotted someone mentioning that Prime 1 may be able to see into any Twilight phase (following from Ephemeral Enchantment affecting any Twilight phase)<br /> <br /> What about Life and Mind, can they see the mind or the life force of someone across Twilight?<br /> <br /> What about Immediate Nimbus? (The current ruling there in my game is that active mage sight doesn't work, but you get a ping on your peripheral mage sight, not that it matters with a Death mage using Suppress Aura)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23542-simonpip","name":"SimonPip","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T17:32:16-08:00","id":1162018,"title":"","content":"You can still be targeted by spells when you are in Twilight. btw. The other thing is to think of things that might have been destroyed (buildings, objects, etc...) in the area as those might have left Twilight remnants of themselves. You can still see MInds and Life patterns with the appropriate Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T19:25:34-08:00","id":1162049,"title":"","content":"Murder isn't required for a building or object to continue a tangible existence within Twilight, just that it was destroyed yet is still remembered (with emotional attachment) by the living. The beloved house a family once called home until it burned down in a fire (they all escaped unharmed) will still exist and be solid in Twilight, as would that hated place of employment were the workers cheered as the city condemned it and knocked it down. Even a child's favorite Tonka truck that his dad backed over can still exist as a solid object in Twilight.<br /> \u200bAlso ghosts aren't the only things that can come from the Underworld, strange and alien entities might infrequently appear within Twilight where they pose a threat to any unfortunate living trespassers.<br /> \u200bYou can also add mysterious anomalies, a building that as far as anyone knows never existed in the material world, strange obelisks that appear at random within Twilight and when they do they send out a pulse or wave that forces any twilight objects (or people/ghosts) to temporarily manifest whether they want to or not. For Rank 1 ghosts this may cause just a harmless sighting, for objects thinking you saw something that just seemed to disappear, but for Mages trapesing through Twilight it dumps them back into the material, forcing them to go through the trouble of casting the spell to return (along with risking Paradox) while in danger of being seen or recorded and that's if they're lucky, unlike the poor fellow who manifested while walking through a wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T03:36:12-08:00","id":1162133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1161970-expanding-on-twilight?p=1162018#post1162018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can still be targeted by spells when you are in Twilight. btw.</div> </div> </div> </div>The phase shift doesn't present a challenge there? If not, the mages in Twilight can basically always target people in realspace, while they would need to be able to sense them somehow (though that becomes simpler if knowing effects look in Twilight as well) to target them. (Originally, I allowed a Death 2 &quot;scrying window&quot; to hear and see through, as well as allow spell casting at remote range, I retracted that as it seemed very powerful)<br /> <br /> I am also wary of making my antagonists too paranoid (in my mind, that could come off as me being a petty GM, if they have anti-my-players spells always running), but preparing a list of running spells an antagonist would have prior to the scene would alleviate that, as I can reassure the players I am not reacting to any clever solutions they come up with during the scene.<br /> <br /> As for the destroyed buildings, that may have been what I was thinking of when I said I remembered something from 1e. Both aspects are good for &quot;populating&quot; Twilight, though, and can make it somewhere you want to go as a destination, not a detour en route to your final destination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23542-simonpip","name":"SimonPip","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T03:42:56-08:00","id":1162134,"title":"","content":"Look at the Death, Mind and Spirit 2 Attainments. Mages with those Attainments have their Peripheral Mage Sights pinged whenever something is in the corresponding Twilight, and can see into the same Twilight by activating Active Mage Sight with that Arcanum. You can also spend a Mana to physically interact with that Arcanum, in case you want to duke it out with Brawl, but that interaction is a two way street.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T05:58:08-08:00","id":1162153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SimonPip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1161970-expanding-on-twilight?p=1162133#post1162133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If not, the mages in Twilight can basically always target people in realspace,</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're in Twilight you can already see and hear people in the material world. I've previously run it the way you describe, but it leaves the issue of how Spirits are able to use their abilities on people if they can't see them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am also wary of making my antagonists too paranoid (in my mind, that could come off as me being a petty GM, if they have anti-my-players spells always running), but preparing a list of running spells an antagonist would have prior to the scene would alleviate that, as I can reassure the players I am not reacting to any clever solutions they come up with during the scene. </div> </div> </div>In the past I've found it useful to use the same tactics on the players, and let their paranoia dictate the level of NPC paranoia. It feels less odd for NPC Awakened to be paranoid, if the players are already jumping at shadows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T12:17:29-08:00","id":1162234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SimonPip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1161970-expanding-on-twilight#post1161970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts could be more numerous, but if there is several ghosts within eyeshot always in Twilight, they become bland scenery. I favor the idea that ghosts are rarer and more &quot;colourful&quot;, having a personality, reliving their death in some detail, but I suppose that could be combined with the faceless drifting spectres drifting through Twilight, to still give some &quot;movement&quot; to Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC 2e does handle this by giving Ghosts a Rank trait like other ephemeral entities. &quot;Literally just scenery&quot; ghosts are Rank 0 and are all over the dang place (including stuff like spectral footprints or bloodstains or other weird spooky phenomena). &quot;People, but trapped reliving the circumstances of their death&quot; Ghosts are Rank 1. &quot;Dead people who are completely coherent and aware and just happen to be dead people/ghosts&quot; are Rank 2. Rank 3 and up start getting into powerful ghosts (and Rank 3 and up are the kind that can become Geists, if they take the necessary steps).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The intangibility is in part solved by Ephemeral Enchantment, perhaps a Death 2 shielding spell to make a wall in the physical realm tangible in Twilight (A Ban would work with Death 2 if you want to create a barrier not tied to a physical object), but I remember, perhaps from 1e, locations tied to the corresponding Arcanum, e.g. a house where someone was murdered, would be tangible in Twilight. This ties nicely together with the more powerful ghosts, where the lair of a powerful ghost will be tangible in Twilight (though it may no longer exist in the real world) </div> </div> </div>Death-Twilight is pretty populated, by things remembered by the living as well, as 2ptTakrill said. There are plenty of things that are tangible in Twilight - as much as in the material world or in the Shadow, often, just in different configurations (as a lot of the newer stuff in the material world doesn't have people attached enough to it to be present in Twilight, while a lot of older stuff that's no longer around in the material world is still very solid and real in Twilight). Ghosts have an entire world to navigate - it's just different from the one solid fleshy people navigate.<br /> <br /> <i>Spirit</i>-Twilight is pretty barren and empty, but that's because most of their stuff is over on the other side of the Gauntlet, and it's mostly populated by a few spirits who've slipped over onto our side.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}